   ],
   "source": "head",
   "order": 0,
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b0"
  },
  {
   "order": 1,
   "class": "Head-fragment",
   "text": "222 ENTOM C",
   "bbox": [
    0.0554,
    0.0473,
    0.5287,
    0.0659
   ],
   "parse_class": "Page-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b1"
  },
  {
   "order": 2,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "a great height; to accomplish which, they climb up some eminence, and are wafted about by the winds, filling the air with their threads. They are destroyed by the sphex and ichneumon.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1285,
    0.0614,
    0.5157,
    0.1248
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b2"
  },
  {
   "order": 3,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Linnaeus has subdivided this genus according to the number and position of their eyes.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1301,
    0.115,
    0.5152,
    0.1523
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b3"
  },
  {
   "order": 4,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "## A. Eyes eight.",
   "bbox": [
    0.2727,
    0.1537,
    0.3778,
    0.1716
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b4"
  },
  {
   "order": 5,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "1. _Eyes placed thus_, ::",
   "bbox": [
    0.2372,
    0.1731,
    0.4154,
    0.1932
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b5"
  },
  {
   "order": 6,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "_fasciata._ Of a silver colour ; the abdomen marked with yellowish bands ; the legs surrounded with brown rings. 48. A native of the island of Madeira.",
   "bbox": [
    0.0548,
    0.1969,
    0.5167,
    0.2394
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b6"
  },
  {
   "order": 7,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "_diadema_ Abdomen nearly globular and reddish ; brown, mark- ed with a white cross composed of dots. 1. A native of Europe, on trees ; it is a very beautiful insect.",
   "bbox": [
    0.0601,
    0.2356,
    0.5183,
    0.2795
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b7"
  },
  {
   "order": 8,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "_aquatica_ Brown ; abdomen oval and of an ash colour ; the back brown, marked with two dots. 39. A native of Europe, in stagnant waters, where it dives to the bot- tom in search of its food. It takes up its winter quar- ters in an empty snail shell, the aperture of which it closes up with a web ; jaws black, claws red.",
   "bbox": [
    0.0612,
    0.2765,
    0.5204,
    0.3614
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b8"
  },
  {
   "order": 9,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "2. _Eyes placed thus_, :",
   "bbox": [
    0.2398,
    0.3606,
    0.4138,
    0.3807
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b9"
  },
  {
   "order": 10,
   "class": "Margin-note",
   "text": "_latro._",
   "bbox": [
    0.0627,
    0.3867,
    0.1029,
    0.4016
   ],
   "parse_class": "Section-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b10"
  },
  {
   "order": 11,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Thorax hairy, and of an ash colour ; the abdominal oval, black, and spotted with red. 95. A native of America ; large, the thorax oval, legs black, thighs pale.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1358,
    0.38,
    0.523,
    0.4418
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b11"
  },
  {
   "order": 12,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "_domesti-_ Abdomen oval and brown, marked with five black spots nearly contiguous, the anterior ones larger than the others. 9. A native of Europe, in houses, and about windows ; feeds chiefly on flies.",
   "bbox": [
    0.0632,
    0.435,
    0.5235,
    0.4961
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b12"
  },
  {
   "order": 13,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "3. _Eyes placed thus_,",
   "bbox": [
    0.2273,
    0.4998,
    0.4148,
    0.5236
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b13"
  },
  {
   "order": 14,
   "class": "Margin-note",
   "text": "_globosa._",
   "bbox": [
    0.0643,
    0.5303,
    0.1343,
    0.5504
   ],
   "parse_class": "Section-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b14"
  },
  {
   "order": 15,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Black ; sides of the abdomen of a blood-red colour. 69. A native of Europe, in meadows.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1385,
    0.5266,
    0.524,
    0.5639
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b15"
  },
  {
   "order": 16,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "4. _Eyes placed thus_,",
   "bbox": [
    0.2456,
    0.5668,
    0.4164,
    0.5877
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b16"
  },
  {
   "order": 17,
   "class": "Margin-note",
   "text": "_argentata._",
   "bbox": [
    0.0648,
    0.5914,
    0.1374,
    0.6152
   ],
   "parse_class": "Section-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b17"
  },
  {
   "order": 18,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Abdomen white, and brown behind, and marked round the edge with six small projections. 70. A native of South America.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1405,
    0.5921,
    0.525,
    0.6405
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b18"
  },
  {
   "order": 19,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "5. _Eyes placed thus_,",
   "bbox": [
    0.2492,
    0.6427,
    0.4243,
    0.6636
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b19"
  },
  {
   "order": 20,
   "class": "Margin-note",
   "text": "_fumigata._",
   "bbox": [
    0.0653,
    0.6725,
    0.1369,
    0.6911
   ],
   "parse_class": "Section-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b20"
  },
  {
   "order": 21,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Abdomen oval and brown, marked at the base with two white dots. 16. A native of Europe, in meadows ; it watches near the nests of the larvae of different insects, and waits their coming out, when it seizes on one after another, and sucks out their substance.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1416,
    0.6687,
    0.5277,
    0.7417
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b21"
  },
  {
   "order": 22,
   "class": "Margin-note",
   "text": "_saccata._",
   "bbox": [
    0.069,
    0.738,
    0.139,
    0.7559
   ],
   "parse_class": "Section-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b22"
  },
  {
   "order": 23,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Abdomen oval, of a brownish colour. 40. A native of Europe, in gardens, and carries its eggs behind it enclosed in a bag ; legs livid, marked with unequal brown rings set close together.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1432,
    0.7365,
    0.5298,
    0.7976
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b23"
  },
  {
   "order": 24,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "_Eyes placed thus_, ::",
   "bbox": [
    0.2575,
    0.7983,
    0.4143,
    0.8155
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b24"
  },
  {
   "order": 25,
   "class": "Margin-note",
   "text": "extensa.",
   "bbox": [
    0.0726,
    0.8206,
    0.129,
    0.8355
   ],
   "parse_class": "Section-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b25"
  },
  {
   "order": 26,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Abdomen long, of a silver colour tinged with green, the legs extended longitudinally. 22. A native of Europe, in woods ; its legs are applied closely to the branches.",
   "bbox": [
    0.1437,
    0.8139,
    0.5308,
    0.8742
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b26"
  },
  {
   "order": 27,
   "class": "Margin-note",
   "text": "_nidulans._",
   "bbox": [
    0.0731,
    0.8727,
    0.1379,
    0.8891
   ],
   "parse_class": "Section-header",
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b27"
  },
  {
   "order": 28,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Shining black ; the abdomen hairy and black. 73. A native of America ; it forms a nest under ground, and spins a large cylindrical web, which is covered with a lid ; its bite is very painful, and frequently oc- casions fever and delirium, which is soon removed by a",
   "bbox": [
    0.1442,
    0.869,
    0.5339,
    0.9442
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-left",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b28"
  },
  {
   "order": 29,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "LEO I.  gentle sudorific ; thorax marked with a large depressed circular spot ; abdomen oval ; legs equal.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5237,
    0.0473,
    0.9137,
    0.0889
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b29"
  },
  {
   "order": 30,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "7. _Eyes placed thus,_ :",
   "bbox": [
    0.6353,
    0.0897,
    0.8111,
    0.1084
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b30"
  },
  {
   "order": 31,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Black, thorax marked with a white line on the back. * dorsal: 79. A native of Britain.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5327,
    0.1135,
    0.9728,
    0.1463
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b31"
  },
  {
   "order": 32,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Marked with triangular black spots on the back of tarantula, the abdomen ; the legs spotted with black. 34. A native of the south of Europe, particularly Italy and Barbary. It is found in caverus in argillaceous soil ; its bite was formerly supposed to be curable by nothing but music ; though it occasions a great deal of pain, it is almost never fatal.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5331,
    0.1418,
    0.9761,
    0.2394
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b32"
  },
  {
   "order": 33,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "8. _Eyes placed thus,_ ...",
   "bbox": [
    0.641,
    0.2408,
    0.8247,
    0.2638
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b33"
  },
  {
   "order": 34,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Oval and oblong ; thorax hairy, white ; abdomen and pulchra. legs black, marked with yellow bands. 32. A native of Europe.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5355,
    0.2661,
    0.969,
    0.313
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b34"
  },
  {
   "order": 35,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "9. _Eyes placed thus,_",
   "bbox": [
    0.625,
    0.322,
    0.7698,
    0.3398
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b35"
  },
  {
   "order": 36,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Black, abdomen oval, forehead white, and leaps on goezii. its prey. 84. It is to be found frequently in woods about Vienna ; abdomen marked with two compressed dots.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5369,
    0.354,
    0.962,
    0.412
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b36"
  },
  {
   "order": 37,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "10. _Eyes placed thus,_ :",
   "bbox": [
    0.639,
    0.409,
    0.8251,
    0.4284
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b37"
  },
  {
   "order": 38,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Thorax orbicular and convex, with a transverse cen-aviculartral excavation. 31. It is a native of South America, among trees, where it preys upon the larger insects, and even small birds, dropping into their nests, and sucking their blood and eggs ; it is of so enormous a size, that its fangs may be compared to the talons of a hawk, and its eyes are very large.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5397,
    0.4336,
    0.9798,
    0.5348
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b38"
  },
  {
   "order": 39,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "11. _Eyes placed thus,_ ...",
   "bbox": [
    0.6414,
    0.543,
    0.82,
    0.5609
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b39"
  },
  {
   "order": 40,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Of a grayish rusty colour, and slightly clouded ; tho-truncate. rax globular, and slightly heart-shaped ; abdomen some-what triangular, and marked with a faint longitudinal cross. 85. A native of Europe, on oak and other trees ; abdomen marked with four impressed dots on the back ; papillae three.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5425,
    0.5742,
    0.9784,
    0.6613
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b40"
  },
  {
   "order": 41,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "12. _Eyes placed thus,_ :",
   "bbox": [
    0.6428,
    0.6703,
    0.8312,
    0.6882
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b41"
  },
  {
   "order": 42,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Abdomen oval, obtusely conic behind, variegated convica. with brown and white ; beneath black. 86. A native of Europe, among bushes ; it spins and spreads out a web, to the surface of which it attaches the insects it has ensnared, after it has sucked out their juice. Tho-rax black, slightly tinged with rusty colour, and nearly double behind ; legs gray, marked with brown rings ; abdomen marked with a whitish spot, beneath resem-bling a horse shoe ; papillae four.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5449,
    0.6949,
    0.9686,
    0.8236
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b42"
  },
  {
   "order": 43,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "13. _Eyes placed thus,_ ...",
   "bbox": [
    0.6245,
    0.8296,
    0.7731,
    0.8481
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b43"
  },
  {
   "order": 44,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Hairy ; body oval, black, variegated with brown. albifras. 99. A native of Europe.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5463,
    0.8474,
    0.9827,
    0.8831
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b44"
  },
  {
   "order": 45,
   "class": "Section-header",
   "text": "B. _Eyes six, placed thus,_ ...",
   "bbox": [
    0.6325,
    0.8854,
    0.8467,
    0.9032
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b45"
  },
  {
   "order": 46,
   "class": "Text",
   "text": "Abdomen greenish, the sides yellow. 30. A na- somies lata.",
   "bbox": [
    0.5481,
    0.904,
    0.9822,
    0.9375
   ],
   "source": "s0-col-right",
   "id": "page-0261-881563669b04:b46"
  },
  {
   "order": 47,
   "class": "Page-footer",
   "text": "C. _Eyes_",
   "bbox": [
    0.873,
    0.9307,
    0.9283,
